{
  "sn12.70:0.1": "Linked Discourses 12.70 ",
  "sn12.70:0.2": "7. The Great Chapter ",
  "sn12.70:0.3": "The Wanderer Susīma ",
  "sn12.70:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "sn12.70:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha in the Bamboo Grove, the squirrels’ feeding ground. ",
  "sn12.70:1.3": "Now at that time the Buddha was honored, respected, revered, venerated, and esteemed. And he received robes, almsfood, lodgings, and medicines and supplies for the sick. ",
  "sn12.70:1.4": "And the mendicant Saṅgha was also honored, respected, revered, venerated, and esteemed. And they received robes, almsfood, lodgings, and medicines and supplies for the sick. ",
  "sn12.70:1.5": "But the wanderers who followed other religions were not honored, respected, revered, venerated, and esteemed. And they didn’t receive robes, almsfood, lodgings, and medicines and supplies for the sick. ",
  "sn12.70:2.1": "Now at that time the wanderer Susīma was residing at Rājagaha together with a large community of wanderers. ",
  "sn12.70:2.2": "Then his community said to Susīma, ",
  "sn12.70:2.3": "“Reverend Susīma, please lead the spiritual life with the ascetic Gotama. ",
  "sn12.70:2.4": "Memorize that teaching and have us recite it with you. ",
  "sn12.70:2.5": "When we’ve memorized it we’ll recite it to the laity. ",
  "sn12.70:2.6": "In this way we too will be honored, respected, revered, venerated, and esteemed. And we’ll receive robes, almsfood, lodgings, and medicines and supplies for the sick.�